WEBVTT

00:00:01.520 --> 00:00:06.190
Galileo Judge

00:00:06.190 --> 00:00:07.940
only to wind up in here again...

00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:09.520
This sucks.

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:13.210
Toscana's gotten really cold.

00:00:13.210 --> 00:00:19.370
Even a place like this has seen its
energy supply cut to forty percent...

00:00:19.670 --> 00:00:22.120
And now we've been hit with quite a cold snap.

00:00:22.120 --> 00:00:24.580
A lot has changed

00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:28.630
in the three months you kids spent on the run.

00:00:28.630 --> 00:00:30.630
This is a case of mistaken arrest!

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:34.510
We haven't done anything to warrant becoming international fugitives!

00:00:34.850 --> 00:00:36.840
If you want to plead not guilty,

00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:39.390
do it in the appropriate place.

00:00:39.730 --> 00:00:41.470
In the appropriate place?

00:00:41.750 --> 00:00:43.810
You three are going to court.

00:00:45.620 --> 00:00:48.020
The trial of the Galileo family.

00:00:54.400 --> 00:01:05.620
koreijou kitai wa shinai to sakki kimeta no ni

00:00:54.400 --> 00:01:05.620
I decided that I won't have any more expectations

00:01:07.460 --> 00:01:13.420
megakuramu juubyou ga sugireba

00:01:07.460 --> 00:01:13.420
But when these dazzling ten seconds pass

00:01:14.130 --> 00:01:20.680
sugu yuragu fukidashita yokan

00:01:14.130 --> 00:01:20.680
I already feel like bursting into laughter

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:22.770
shinkuromanika

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:22.770
Synchromanica

00:01:22.770 --> 00:01:24.310
itsu no ma ni ka

00:01:22.770 --> 00:01:24.310
Before I know it

00:01:24.310 --> 00:01:27.480
kono koe wa negai no you da

00:01:24.310 --> 00:01:27.480
This voice starts to sound like a wish

00:01:27.480 --> 00:01:33.780
tanjun ni ikanai mirai ga tokimeki no sumika

00:01:27.480 --> 00:01:33.780
The future isn't simple, but it brings excitement

00:01:33.780 --> 00:01:40.280
boku no mimi wa dareka no yume da

00:01:33.780 --> 00:01:40.280
I can hear someone's dream

00:01:40.280 --> 00:01:47.250
kotoba ni wa shinain da subete

00:01:40.280 --> 00:01:47.250
But I won't say any of it out loud

00:01:56.590 --> 00:02:00.050
tsuujiaeba hiraku tobira

00:01:56.590 --> 00:02:00.050
If we understand one another, the gate opens

00:02:00.050 --> 00:02:02.390
shinkuromanika

00:02:00.050 --> 00:02:02.390
Synchromanica

00:02:03.260 --> 00:02:06.520
tsuujiaeba hiraku tobira

00:02:03.260 --> 00:02:06.520
If we understand one another, the gate opens

00:02:06.520 --> 00:02:08.560
shinkuromanika

00:02:06.520 --> 00:02:08.560
Synchromanica

00:02:13.020 --> 00:02:16.780
kimi wa ikeru shinkuro

00:02:13.020 --> 00:02:16.780
The synchrony of your life

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:23.620
Why does Messier exist, Roberto?

00:02:23.940 --> 00:02:26.680
Given the circumstances, I had no choice.

00:02:27.510 --> 00:02:30.710
We could hardly massacre Interpol agents.

00:02:31.670 --> 00:02:33.800
I want to meet them.

00:02:37.330 --> 00:02:42.470
This is our first face-to-face meeting, Galileo sisters.

00:02:42.470 --> 00:02:44.720
What does an evil CEO want with us?

00:02:46.230 --> 00:02:49.230
There is no question that you will be found guilty.

00:02:49.230 --> 00:02:52.560
However, I will give you a chance.

00:02:53.410 --> 00:02:58.070
If you tell me where the Galileo Tesoro is,
I can have you set free.

00:02:58.070 --> 00:03:00.000
I knew that was it.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:03.040
My offer is a fairly straightforward one.

00:03:04.020 --> 00:03:06.080
We cannot give you the Tesoro.

00:03:06.080 --> 00:03:09.500
We have no intention of telling you anything about the Tesoro, either.

00:03:11.010 --> 00:03:15.250
Then enjoy spending the rest of your lives in prison.

00:03:18.180 --> 00:03:21.760
Your daughters are pretty stubborn.

00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:25.010
I do not recall ever having daughters.

00:03:30.290 --> 00:03:34.020
What do you intend to do with me, Roberto?

00:03:38.030 --> 00:03:39.320
Who's there?

00:03:43.340 --> 00:03:44.690
It's open?

00:03:52.130 --> 00:03:53.750
You've found an attorney?

00:03:53.750 --> 00:03:56.130
Yeah, just one.

00:04:02.620 --> 00:04:04.930
Sir, thank you for taking our case.

00:04:06.930 --> 00:04:09.180
Will he be okay?

00:04:09.180 --> 00:04:11.390
Does he even know he's here?

00:04:16.520 --> 00:04:17.480
Hey!

00:04:17.480 --> 00:04:19.570
These are the Moon sketches!

00:04:19.570 --> 00:04:21.940
Why does this guy have them?

00:04:21.940 --> 00:04:24.030
The spoiled brat took them, didn't he?

00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:27.120
A certain lady gave them to me.

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:29.300
Who was this lady?

00:04:29.300 --> 00:04:30.040
Oh...

00:04:30.040 --> 00:04:33.790
Uh, I don't remember.

00:04:33.790 --> 00:04:36.790
Are they that important?

00:04:36.790 --> 00:04:38.500
They're <i>super</i> important!

00:04:38.500 --> 00:04:42.260
O-Oh, she asked me to give this to you kids, as well.

00:04:55.050 --> 00:04:57.480
So that was the trick?

00:04:57.850 --> 00:05:01.530
"When we parted ways, we promised to follow our own paths.

00:05:01.530 --> 00:05:06.690
In the hope that it will help you,
I shall leave you these manufacturing methods.

00:05:06.690 --> 00:05:09.990
I was unable to complete it,

00:05:09.990 --> 00:05:12.320
but I am certain you can.

00:05:12.950 --> 00:05:15.260
I want you to try your best.

00:05:15.260 --> 00:05:18.810
I will not forget you...
You, whose name contains the Moon."

00:05:21.150 --> 00:05:22.740
Galileo...

00:05:22.740 --> 00:05:23.910
Hocchii?

00:05:25.620 --> 00:05:28.580
This seems to be a love letter.

00:05:28.580 --> 00:05:30.220
I wonder for whom he wrote it.

00:05:34.090 --> 00:05:35.730
We can't stop here.

00:05:38.230 --> 00:05:40.690
We might've succeeded in collecting them,

00:05:40.690 --> 00:05:42.780
but we haven't learned the secret of the inheritance.

00:05:42.780 --> 00:05:46.240
Doesn't moonlight affect it like the others?

00:05:46.550 --> 00:05:50.740
Galileo's message is all that appears... Nothing else.

00:05:51.050 --> 00:05:55.250
But when did you manage to transfer the Tesoro inside Picco Rosso, anyway?

00:05:55.950 --> 00:06:00.080
When we were in Germany, Grande Rosso told me

00:06:00.490 --> 00:06:03.090
that Anna-san was acting suspicious.

00:06:04.270 --> 00:06:07.260
Ever since the Tesoro first activated in that Russian hospital,

00:06:07.630 --> 00:06:10.340
I've kept it hidden in Picco Rosso, just to be safe.

00:06:10.340 --> 00:06:13.330
Why didn't you tell us?

00:06:13.330 --> 00:06:16.600
Because Anna-san was always with us...

00:06:16.600 --> 00:06:21.360
Actually, when did you swap Picco Rosso with a mecha goldfish, anyway?

00:06:21.360 --> 00:06:24.360
More importantly, this sixth sketch...

00:06:24.360 --> 00:06:29.990
It would've been nice if he'd left a hint or two where we'd found it.

00:06:29.990 --> 00:06:31.310
A hint...

00:06:32.370 --> 00:06:34.870
Oh! I get it now!

00:06:34.870 --> 00:06:36.700
What, Hocchibi?

00:06:36.700 --> 00:06:39.870
Haa-nee, Kaa-nee, I figured out the secret!

00:06:41.920 --> 00:06:41.960
Energy problem : trial of the century

00:06:42.930 --> 00:06:46.880
<i>The highly public trial that has garnered
international attention is finally about to begin.</i>

00:06:46.880 --> 00:06:51.280
<i>It pits Adnimoon, a world leader in energy development,</i>

00:06:51.280 --> 00:06:56.420
<i>against three sisters accused of stealing methane hydrate from Adnimoon.</i>

00:06:55.180 --> 00:06:57.560
Will we get what we asked you for in time?

00:06:56.850 --> 00:06:59.500
<i>The defendants are not just anyone, either.</i>

00:06:58.070 --> 00:07:00.370
There hasn't been any response.

00:06:59.500 --> 00:07:02.490
<i>They are said to be descendants of Galileo Galilei.</i>

00:07:00.370 --> 00:07:02.490
Perhaps it was impossible.

00:07:02.490 --> 00:07:03.940
I see.

00:07:03.940 --> 00:07:07.440
<i>How will this trial end?</i>

00:07:07.440 --> 00:07:08.940
<i>We won't be able to take our eyes off it!</i>

00:07:16.150 --> 00:07:17.490
Court is now in session!

00:07:19.250 --> 00:07:21.080
First, may I direct your attention to this.

00:07:21.820 --> 00:07:23.630
Hozuki Ferrari's act of violence

00:07:23.630 --> 00:07:26.210
caused considerable damage to the Toscana Police Station.

00:07:26.210 --> 00:07:30.510
Repairs took two months and an enormous sum of money.

00:07:31.110 --> 00:07:34.600
This incident could be called one of the

00:07:34.600 --> 00:07:36.890
most vicious criminal acts in the history of Toscana.

00:07:36.890 --> 00:07:37.760
Objection!

00:07:38.110 --> 00:07:41.020
The defendant has not been given permission to speak.

00:07:41.020 --> 00:07:44.690
As long as the defendant has an attorney,

00:07:44.690 --> 00:07:47.570
anyone can speak for the defense.

00:07:47.570 --> 00:07:48.530
Am I wrong?

00:07:48.980 --> 00:07:50.030
Sir!

00:07:53.060 --> 00:07:55.030
I suppose... Permission granted.

00:07:55.500 --> 00:07:59.420
It is true that we broke out of the Toscana Police Station.

00:07:59.420 --> 00:08:03.420
It is also true that we caused damage to the building in the process.

00:08:03.420 --> 00:08:06.100
We do not intend to refute that.

00:08:06.100 --> 00:08:10.050
However, circumstances at the time made it necessary.

00:08:10.340 --> 00:08:13.840
Then your claim is that crimes are
permissible if the cause is justified?

00:08:13.840 --> 00:08:18.310
Your honor, the defendant is simply trying to obscure the issue.

00:08:18.310 --> 00:08:19.650
Objection!

00:08:19.650 --> 00:08:21.560
I am not trying to obscure the issue!

00:08:21.560 --> 00:08:23.380
Overruled.

00:08:23.380 --> 00:08:27.410
We were unjustly arrested! We'd done nothing!

00:08:27.410 --> 00:08:29.250
Your objection has been overruled.

00:08:29.250 --> 00:08:31.320
You have no further right to speak.

00:08:31.660 --> 00:08:34.800
You studied law at university,
intending to become a prosecutor,

00:08:34.800 --> 00:08:37.070
but you lack even that basic knowledge?

00:08:37.070 --> 00:08:39.080
Please hear us out!

00:08:39.080 --> 00:08:41.450
Order!

00:08:41.450 --> 00:08:45.120
Although, it does appear that your academic performance was rather poor.

00:08:47.570 --> 00:08:50.840
Do you remember who did that to you?

00:08:52.090 --> 00:08:53.690
Who was it?

00:08:56.840 --> 00:09:02.060
Hozuki Ferrari-san, this man claims that you caused him bodily harm.

00:09:02.060 --> 00:09:03.350
Is this true?

00:09:04.390 --> 00:09:06.100
It's true.

00:09:06.100 --> 00:09:09.610
But he suddenly attacked me, so I had no choice.

00:09:09.610 --> 00:09:11.110
A little girl like her was that violent?

00:09:11.110 --> 00:09:13.000
How horrible.

00:09:14.420 --> 00:09:18.120
You used a high-voltage weapon called a stun gun launcher, correct?

00:09:18.550 --> 00:09:19.620
Yes...

00:09:19.620 --> 00:09:23.560
This powered suit, which was used in the police station attack

00:09:23.560 --> 00:09:26.120
was developed by you as well, correct?

00:09:26.470 --> 00:09:27.370
Yes.

00:09:27.370 --> 00:09:28.420
Objection!

00:09:28.420 --> 00:09:31.130
She had no choice but to use it to save us!

00:09:31.420 --> 00:09:35.680
I have heard that you also developed this weapon of mass destruction.

00:09:35.680 --> 00:09:37.130
Is that correct?

00:09:37.130 --> 00:09:38.640
It isn't a weapon!

00:09:38.640 --> 00:09:42.240
Is it true that it was you, Hozuki Ferrari-san,

00:09:42.240 --> 00:09:45.640
who developed this weapon and armed it with missiles and machine guns?

00:09:47.570 --> 00:09:49.650
It's true.

00:09:51.150 --> 00:09:54.810
Hozuki Ferrari has created several weapons with great destructive capabilities

00:09:54.810 --> 00:09:58.780
and used them to carry out heists and murders one might attribute to air pirates.

00:09:59.230 --> 00:10:01.870
For instance, a certain city in the Netherlands...

00:10:01.870 --> 00:10:04.290
No, wait! That wasn't me!

00:10:04.290 --> 00:10:08.330
We have an eyewitness testimony that says a goldfish mecha attacked them.

00:10:08.330 --> 00:10:11.290
The purpose of the attack was, again, the theft of methane hydrate.

00:10:11.750 --> 00:10:12.810
That's a lie!

00:10:12.810 --> 00:10:13.930
What the hell?

00:10:13.930 --> 00:10:14.920
It's a setup.

00:10:14.920 --> 00:10:16.850
Everyone's being duped!

00:10:20.760 --> 00:10:23.260
The bastards have falsified evidence.

00:10:25.450 --> 00:10:28.270
I believe everyone here is now fully aware

00:10:28.270 --> 00:10:31.770
of how reprehensible these three criminals are.

00:10:32.520 --> 00:10:34.570
Hey, wake up, geezer!

00:10:34.570 --> 00:10:36.330
We're in a crisis now!

00:10:37.410 --> 00:10:39.030
Oh, in that case...

00:10:42.460 --> 00:10:45.290
Please drink this, and take a breather.

00:10:45.290 --> 00:10:46.160
Yeah, right!

00:10:46.160 --> 00:10:47.790
Just do your job!

00:10:50.300 --> 00:10:51.290
Hey!

00:10:51.940 --> 00:10:52.790
This is...

00:10:54.820 --> 00:10:56.800
What is it?

00:10:58.650 --> 00:11:02.430
Your honor, allow me to submit evidence!

00:11:02.430 --> 00:11:03.300
Hazu-nee?

00:11:06.260 --> 00:11:10.040
Are you all familiar with this large weapon?

00:11:10.970 --> 00:11:14.310
It is an Aza Iron, the destructive weapon

00:11:14.310 --> 00:11:18.570
air pirates are said to have used in
methane hydrate attacks worldwide.

00:11:18.870 --> 00:11:22.450
Francesco-san, do you recognize this transporter?

00:11:22.970 --> 00:11:24.160
I do not.

00:11:24.160 --> 00:11:25.910
That can't be true.

00:11:25.910 --> 00:11:28.450
The documents here clearly state

00:11:28.810 --> 00:11:32.790
that it is the <i>Gassendi</i>, an Aza Iron transport belonging to the Adnimoon Company.

00:11:34.020 --> 00:11:37.500
Furthermore, from this is footage taken inside the <i>Gassendi</i>

00:11:37.500 --> 00:11:40.470
One can clearly see that it stores large numbers of Aza Iron units.

00:11:40.470 --> 00:11:43.260
Francesco-san, you're aware of this, aren't you?

00:11:43.260 --> 00:11:44.700
I... I am not.

00:11:44.700 --> 00:11:46.470
You're an amazing attorney!

00:11:47.240 --> 00:11:50.480
These documents also clearly state the location of the factory

00:11:48.030 --> 00:11:50.480
Why did you have these documents?

00:11:50.480 --> 00:11:52.210
where the Aza Irons were constructed.

00:11:52.210 --> 00:11:56.230
Do you still claim ignorance, Francesco-san?

00:11:56.870 --> 00:11:58.960
As the physical evidence suggests,

00:11:58.960 --> 00:12:03.210
Adnimoon developed and used the destructive Aza Irons

00:12:03.210 --> 00:12:05.990
to seize methane hydrate worldwide

00:12:05.990 --> 00:12:09.370
and to frame air pirates for their crimes.

00:12:09.370 --> 00:12:12.240
All to increase their own company's profits!

00:12:13.250 --> 00:12:14.500
Order!

00:12:14.790 --> 00:12:19.710
Your honor, her claims have no relevance to the case.

00:12:19.710 --> 00:12:21.840
How are they not relevant?

00:12:21.840 --> 00:12:23.930
Only matters pertaining

00:12:23.930 --> 00:12:26.560
to the Ferrari sisters' actions are subject to debate in this court!

00:12:26.560 --> 00:12:28.390
Objection, your honor!

00:12:28.390 --> 00:12:29.100
Objection!

00:12:29.570 --> 00:12:31.320
Overruled.

00:12:31.320 --> 00:12:33.100
Please return to your seat.

00:12:33.740 --> 00:12:38.640
I agree that these claims are not relevant to this case.

00:12:38.640 --> 00:12:39.730
But...

00:12:39.730 --> 00:12:40.610
Your honor,

00:12:41.250 --> 00:12:44.610
we'd like to call our final witness to the stand.

00:12:44.610 --> 00:12:46.380
Final witness?

00:12:46.380 --> 00:12:47.610
Proceed.

00:12:47.610 --> 00:12:50.620
The prosecution may bring in its witness.

00:12:55.120 --> 00:12:56.290
Mama!

00:12:56.290 --> 00:12:58.130
She's okay!

00:13:00.750 --> 00:13:04.130
I must apologize to everyone here.

00:13:04.130 --> 00:13:08.640
My daughters' crimes are my own responsibility.

00:13:08.640 --> 00:13:09.440
Huh?

00:13:09.440 --> 00:13:10.350
Mama?

00:13:10.350 --> 00:13:13.640
Hozuki has always concealed her rare talents.

00:13:13.640 --> 00:13:17.400
But now they have been revealed to the world through criminal acts.

00:13:17.400 --> 00:13:21.150
I failed to guide and educate her on the difference between good and evil...

00:13:21.150 --> 00:13:21.940
Mama,

00:13:21.940 --> 00:13:22.650
listen to yourself!

00:13:22.650 --> 00:13:26.400
I'd like Hozuki to recognize the gravity of her crimes

00:13:26.400 --> 00:13:28.030
and to take the appropriate responsibility.

00:13:28.470 --> 00:13:31.280
As her parent, that is my wish.

00:13:31.770 --> 00:13:33.290
This is bull!

00:13:33.290 --> 00:13:35.410
What are you saying, Mama?

00:13:35.410 --> 00:13:36.960
Hocchibi isn't like that...

00:13:36.960 --> 00:13:38.290
That isn't who she is!

00:13:38.290 --> 00:13:40.840
Sure, Hocchibi can be reckless.

00:13:40.840 --> 00:13:42.170
She's weird.

00:13:42.170 --> 00:13:44.340
I have no idea what she's thinking.

00:13:44.340 --> 00:13:47.640
And I wouldn't want to be her friend.

00:13:47.640 --> 00:13:50.800
But she isn't the kind of girl who'd hurt anyone without cause!

00:13:51.130 --> 00:13:56.060
The mecha Hocchibi made has saved us so many times.

00:13:56.060 --> 00:13:58.980
Don't talk about her like that...

00:13:58.980 --> 00:14:00.060
Kaa-nee...

00:14:00.410 --> 00:14:03.690
Your honor, it is an indisputable fact

00:14:03.690 --> 00:14:06.950
that her dangerous inventions have harmed many people.

00:14:06.950 --> 00:14:07.570
Objection!

00:14:07.570 --> 00:14:08.700
There are witnesses...

00:14:08.700 --> 00:14:10.070
We have evidence!

00:14:11.580 --> 00:14:13.530
What further proof do you need?

00:14:13.530 --> 00:14:15.580
Please make a ruling, your honor.

00:14:17.950 --> 00:14:19.580
You may have a point.

00:14:19.580 --> 00:14:21.600
How could you?

00:14:21.600 --> 00:14:23.070
Damn it...

00:14:24.050 --> 00:14:25.590
Objection.

00:14:34.740 --> 00:14:36.730
This farce has gone on long enough.

00:14:36.730 --> 00:14:37.770
No way.

00:14:37.770 --> 00:14:38.480
Papa!

00:14:38.480 --> 00:14:39.620
And who are you?

00:14:39.620 --> 00:14:42.480
Geshio Ferrari, the girls' father

00:14:42.780 --> 00:14:44.730
and Sylvia's husband.

00:14:44.730 --> 00:14:45.800
Hozuki!

00:14:49.570 --> 00:14:52.070
I found it with a little help.

00:14:52.070 --> 00:14:53.580
Thanks, Papa!

00:14:57.890 --> 00:15:02.080
Although it is true that Hozuki has not yet fully matured,

00:15:02.080 --> 00:15:06.180
she would never use her talents to pursue her own interests.

00:15:06.180 --> 00:15:08.210
I guarantee that

00:15:08.210 --> 00:15:09.720
as her mother.

00:15:09.720 --> 00:15:10.720
Mama!

00:15:10.720 --> 00:15:16.370
I was not the best mother to my daughters.

00:15:16.370 --> 00:15:20.230
I do not delude myself for an instant that they harbor great contempt for me.

00:15:20.230 --> 00:15:24.690
But I still reserve the right to have faith in my daughters.

00:15:24.690 --> 00:15:29.360
Because you are Galileo Galilei's descendants.

00:15:30.110 --> 00:15:30.990
Sylvie...

00:15:30.990 --> 00:15:31.990
Mama!

00:15:33.730 --> 00:15:37.870
I say with utter conviction that my daughters are innocent.

00:15:37.870 --> 00:15:39.290
Don't be so foolish!

00:15:39.290 --> 00:15:41.500
You believe in them because you're their mother?

00:15:41.500 --> 00:15:43.750
What do you even base this opinion on?

00:15:43.750 --> 00:15:47.960
Unfortunately, trust within a family needs no basis.

00:15:47.960 --> 00:15:51.470
Instead, I'd like to present something to the court.

00:15:54.990 --> 00:15:57.720
This is evidence that Adnimoon has used

00:15:57.720 --> 00:16:02.020
an illegal organization called Messier to secretly conduct criminal acts.

00:16:02.980 --> 00:16:06.860
It contains irrefutable proof that the destructive acts

00:16:06.860 --> 00:16:10.780
my daughters are accused of were, in fact, Messier's actions.

00:16:11.130 --> 00:16:12.570
Such evidence exists?

00:16:12.570 --> 00:16:13.410
That's inadmissible!

00:16:13.910 --> 00:16:17.490
It's highly probable that evidence has been forged...

00:16:17.490 --> 00:16:21.290
You can rule that out by verifying the file names, dates, and times of creation

00:16:21.290 --> 00:16:25.460
with the originals on Francesco's personal computer.

00:16:26.370 --> 00:16:27.540
Sylvia!

00:16:27.540 --> 00:16:28.960
When did your memory return?

00:16:28.960 --> 00:16:31.140
When I was injured, I had a realization.

00:16:31.140 --> 00:16:33.640
I realized that to reveal the truth about Adnimoon,

00:16:33.640 --> 00:16:36.250
I'd have to work from the inside.

00:16:36.250 --> 00:16:37.220
And to do that...

00:16:37.220 --> 00:16:39.720
You pretended to have amnesia.

00:16:40.150 --> 00:16:44.730
Your honor, I'd like to add that as additional evidence.

00:16:48.610 --> 00:16:52.400
Will you answer questions about the evidence presented in court?

00:16:52.400 --> 00:16:53.820
No comment.

00:16:53.820 --> 00:16:54.650
Out of the way!

00:17:00.100 --> 00:17:04.080
Roberto...

00:17:04.530 --> 00:17:06.040
Why?

00:17:06.040 --> 00:17:07.040
Drop your weapon!

00:17:07.040 --> 00:17:09.710
I love you, Papa.

00:17:09.710 --> 00:17:11.530
You're under arrest for murder!

00:17:15.630 --> 00:17:17.590
I'm so glad, Mama...

00:17:17.590 --> 00:17:20.720
Idiot, don't you know how much we worried about you?

00:17:20.720 --> 00:17:21.810
Sorry.

00:17:21.810 --> 00:17:24.180
I heard about you guys.

00:17:24.180 --> 00:17:27.850
While I was evading Messier's pursuit, I eventually made contact with Sylvia

00:17:27.850 --> 00:17:30.140
and learned what she was doing.

00:17:30.140 --> 00:17:33.180
Your father was secretly helping me.

00:17:33.180 --> 00:17:35.360
Not bad.

00:17:35.360 --> 00:17:38.430
<i>She</i> was also helping us.

00:17:41.090 --> 00:17:42.240
Anna-san!

00:17:42.240 --> 00:17:43.660
Anhedo-san.

00:17:42.240 --> 00:17:43.660
Anna-san!

00:17:43.660 --> 00:17:44.830
Thank you for your help.

00:17:44.830 --> 00:17:47.580
You are this family's savior.

00:17:48.010 --> 00:17:52.090
Weren't you the one who helped me escape from my prison?

00:17:52.090 --> 00:17:53.840
What's that?

00:17:53.840 --> 00:17:56.550
The locations of the Moon sketches, the hourglass strap,

00:17:56.550 --> 00:17:59.390
and the telescope were all written here.

00:18:04.190 --> 00:18:06.360
What are you looking at, Hocchii?

00:18:06.360 --> 00:18:09.130
Don't you use telescopes to look at the sky?

00:18:10.390 --> 00:18:11.730
I get it...

00:18:11.730 --> 00:18:14.280
Hozuki-chan, this is it, right?

00:18:14.940 --> 00:18:16.280
I knew I'd find it!

00:18:16.280 --> 00:18:17.240
Seriously?

00:18:17.240 --> 00:18:18.280
Let me see!

00:18:18.700 --> 00:18:21.530
The Galileo Tesoro is incomplete...

00:18:22.030 --> 00:18:24.130
He learned that its activation causes a chemical reaction

00:18:24.130 --> 00:18:26.810
that in turn triggers a certain phenomenon.

00:18:26.810 --> 00:18:28.040
Phenomenon?

00:18:28.410 --> 00:18:30.960
That's why Galileo never went public

00:18:30.960 --> 00:18:34.460
and left only a small amount to us.

00:18:35.560 --> 00:18:37.240
That's awesome...

00:18:37.240 --> 00:18:39.860
Now that's what you call treasure.

00:18:40.690 --> 00:18:41.970
Sir?

00:18:41.970 --> 00:18:44.010
You still don't get it?

00:18:49.990 --> 00:18:51.020
It's me!

00:18:51.020 --> 00:18:52.250
GanyBoss?

00:18:52.250 --> 00:18:53.650
You're alive?!

00:18:54.030 --> 00:18:55.690
Don't just kill me off.

00:18:55.690 --> 00:18:57.110
You know,

00:18:57.110 --> 00:19:00.450
it's nice that you gave us the sketches and the evidence,

00:19:00.450 --> 00:19:02.820
but wasn't there a better way to do it?

00:19:02.820 --> 00:19:04.530
Wasn't this exciting, though?

00:19:04.530 --> 00:19:06.740
Court's like a show!

00:19:07.730 --> 00:19:09.790
So you helped us!

00:19:09.790 --> 00:19:11.690
Thanks, GanyBoss-san.

00:19:12.460 --> 00:19:15.670
Oh, and about compensating you for the tailplane I destroyed...

00:19:15.670 --> 00:19:17.670
I don't need any compensation.

00:19:17.990 --> 00:19:19.340
I have my...

00:19:20.930 --> 00:19:22.300
reward right here!

00:19:22.300 --> 00:19:25.010
This is the treasure of the century.

00:19:25.010 --> 00:19:25.890
Idiot!

00:19:25.890 --> 00:19:28.050
Do you even know what that is?

00:19:29.210 --> 00:19:31.100
Bye, Bambina!

00:19:35.870 --> 00:19:36.630
Later!

00:19:41.230 --> 00:19:43.570
What has he done?!

00:19:43.570 --> 00:19:45.910
I can make more. It's okay.

00:19:45.910 --> 00:19:46.830
What?

00:19:46.830 --> 00:19:49.330
I have the records right here.

00:19:50.190 --> 00:19:51.330
You're right.

00:19:59.050 --> 00:20:02.650
The seventh sketch was just a ruse, right?

00:20:02.650 --> 00:20:04.550
I want to make sure...

00:20:04.550 --> 00:20:07.060
Hocchii, did you find it?

00:20:07.060 --> 00:20:09.430
It should be around here—

00:20:09.620 --> 00:20:10.950
Hocchii!

00:20:09.620 --> 00:20:10.950
Hocchibi!

00:20:11.740 --> 00:20:13.210
Are you okay?!

00:20:13.210 --> 00:20:14.440
I... I'm fine.

00:20:14.740 --> 00:20:16.270
Ow...

00:20:17.310 --> 00:20:18.940
Oh, there it is!

00:20:19.570 --> 00:20:22.200
This is the junk from the attic.

00:20:22.200 --> 00:20:25.320
You really think the seventh sketch is in <i>here</i>?

00:20:25.320 --> 00:20:26.820
I think so.

00:20:26.820 --> 00:20:27.910
Let's do this.

00:20:33.150 --> 00:20:34.870
There's the seventh sketch!

00:20:35.170 --> 00:20:38.880
The reveal had better not be that there was actually another inheritance.

00:20:41.110 --> 00:20:42.800
Galileo...

00:20:42.800 --> 00:20:44.010
What's this?

00:20:44.010 --> 00:20:46.180
It isn't a Moon sketch.

00:20:46.180 --> 00:20:48.290
This looks like Hocchii.

00:20:48.290 --> 00:20:52.600
And this kind of looks like the <i>Galileo</i>, too...

00:20:54.030 --> 00:20:57.110
Why didn't I realize it before?

00:20:57.110 --> 00:20:58.360
Before?

00:20:58.630 --> 00:21:03.330
I made the <i>Galileo</i> by modifying the same blueprint as this one.

00:21:03.330 --> 00:21:07.030
The one you said you found in the attic?

00:21:08.660 --> 00:21:12.080
I guess we should complete the Galileo Tesoro,

00:21:12.080 --> 00:21:14.370
as descendants of Galileo.

00:21:14.370 --> 00:21:15.290
Yeah.

00:21:15.290 --> 00:21:17.290
You can do it, Hocchibi...

00:21:18.790 --> 00:21:19.790
Yeah!

00:21:19.790 --> 00:21:21.050
Let's go.

00:21:21.510 --> 00:21:23.550
Grandpa will be so surprised!

00:21:23.930 --> 00:21:26.010
You promised him that you'd visit again

00:21:26.010 --> 00:21:27.800
with the whole family, right?

00:21:31.510 --> 00:21:33.980
Off to Japan once more!

00:21:34.630 --> 00:21:36.730
Launch the <i>Galileo</i>!

00:21:36.980 --> 00:21:41.070
asa ga kuru no mo kizukanai mama

00:21:36.980 --> 00:21:41.070
I used to not even notice the sun rising

00:21:41.070 --> 00:21:44.900
nagareboshi wo sagashiteta

00:21:41.070 --> 00:21:44.900
As I was looking for shooting stars

00:21:44.900 --> 00:21:51.910
ano koro no you ni sora wo miageru koto mo shinakunatteta

00:21:44.900 --> 00:21:51.910
But now I no longer look up at the sky like that

00:21:51.910 --> 00:21:57.040
nande mo nai negaigoto datte

00:21:51.910 --> 00:21:57.040
I don't even remember the wishes I wanted to make

00:21:57.040 --> 00:22:01.420
hitori ja nai kono basho nara

00:21:57.040 --> 00:22:01.420
That place where I'm not alone

00:22:01.420 --> 00:22:06.720
kitto mata mitsukedaseru

00:22:01.420 --> 00:22:06.720
I'm sure I can find it again

00:22:06.720 --> 00:22:14.680
ima yozora ni kagayaku hoshikuzu no naka kara

00:22:06.720 --> 00:22:14.680
Among the stardust shining in the night sky

00:22:14.680 --> 00:22:23.070
wasurekakete ita itsuka no mirai wo sagasou

00:22:14.680 --> 00:22:23.070
I'll search for the future that I had almost forgotten

00:22:23.070 --> 00:22:30.200
me wo korashite hitosuji no hikari ga

00:22:23.070 --> 00:22:30.200
As I strain my eyes to find that single beam of light

00:22:30.200 --> 00:22:42.340
oto mo naku nagareru sono kiseki oikakete yukou

00:22:30.200 --> 00:22:42.340
I'll chase after that silently flowing miracle
